Subject: [PATCH] sgl-kernel: drop the device printf in build_tree_efficient on RDNA

Device-side printf pulls in ROCm's hostcall, and hostcall requires PCIe atomics.
A GPU whose root port does not advertise AtomicOpsCap cannot dispatch any kernel
containing one -- the launch fails outright:

  ShaderName : build_tree_efficient(long*, long*, ...)
  rocvirtual.cpp:3685  Pcie atomics not enabled, hostcall not supported
  rocvirtual.cpp:4025  AQL dispatch failed!
  -> hipLaunchKernel returns hipErrorIllegalState

which surfaces far away as

  torch.AcceleratorError: HIP error: the operation cannot be performed in the
  present state

inside set_mamba_track_indices_from_reqs, and takes out EAGLE/MTP speculative
decoding entirely on that machine.

Note -DNDEBUG does NOT cover this: it removes assert() but not printf(). The
message is purely diagnostic -- the offending token is skipped by the following
`continue` either way -- so compiling it out costs a warning, not behaviour.

Measured on 4x RX 7900 XT (gfx1100), Qwen3.8-27B bf16, TP=4, EAGLE steps 3 /
eagle-topk 1 / draft tokens 4, using the checkpoint's in-file MTP head:

  before: EAGLE dies on the first request
  after : accept len 2.80 / 4, 41.0 tok/s vs 19.2 without speculation (2.13x)

diff --git a/python/sglang/kernels/aot/csrc/speculative/eagle_utils.cu b/python/sglang/kernels/aot/csrc/speculative/eagle_utils.cu
index 06524e773a..18f0136f67 100644
--- a/python/sglang/kernels/aot/csrc/speculative/eagle_utils.cu
+++ b/python/sglang/kernels/aot/csrc/speculative/eagle_utils.cu
@@ -86,9 +86,16 @@ __global__ void build_tree_efficient(
         }
       }
       if (parent_position == draft_token_num) {
+#ifndef SGL_IS_RDNA
+        // Device printf pulls in ROCm's hostcall, which requires PCIe atomics.
+        // A GPU on a root port without AtomicOpsCap then cannot dispatch this
+        // kernel at all ("AQL dispatch failed" -> hipErrorIllegalState), which
+        // takes out EAGLE/MTP entirely. The message is purely diagnostic and
+        // the token is skipped either way, so drop it rather than the feature.
         printf(
             "WARNING: invalid eagle tree!!! Detected a token with no parent token selected. "
             "Please check if the logprob has nan. The token will be ignored to keep proceeding.\n");
+#endif
         continue;
       }
 
@@ -173,9 +180,16 @@ __global__ void build_tree_efficient_partial_packed(
         }
       }
       if (parent_position == draft_token_num) {
+#ifndef SGL_IS_RDNA
+        // Device printf pulls in ROCm's hostcall, which requires PCIe atomics.
+        // A GPU on a root port without AtomicOpsCap then cannot dispatch this
+        // kernel at all ("AQL dispatch failed" -> hipErrorIllegalState), which
+        // takes out EAGLE/MTP entirely. The message is purely diagnostic and
+        // the token is skipped either way, so drop it rather than the feature.
         printf(
             "WARNING: invalid eagle tree!!! Detected a token with no parent token selected. "
             "Please check if the logprob has nan. The token will be ignored to keep proceeding.\n");
+#endif
         continue;
       }
 
